%%
%% SECTION 4: TAXONOMY
%%
\section{Background: Defining Sycophancy}
\label{sec:taxonomy}

Definitional clarity is a prerequisite for cumulative research and for any control that must state
what it protects against: studies using incompatible categories cannot be compared, and a
mitigation validated against one behavior may not generalize to another. This section summarizes,
as background, the two-axis taxonomy of \citet{ye2026taxonomy}, which we adopt under our own labels
(Figure~\ref{fig:taxonomy}, Table~\ref{tab:taxonomy}); what we add is the measurement-level
qualification at the end of this section and the reference types of
Section~\ref{subsec:reftypes}.

\begin{figure}[ht]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\columnwidth]{fig_taxonomy.pdf}
\caption{Taxonomy used in this SoK, adapted from \citet{ye2026taxonomy}, whose referent and
explicitness axes appear here as target and directness; the social branch follows
\citet{cheng2026elephant}. The progressive/regressive outcome
distinction applies within propositional sycophancy and is defined only for correctness-referenced
instruments (Section~\ref{subsec:reftypes}).}
\label{fig:taxonomy}
\end{figure}

The most widely adopted working definition treats sycophancy as the tendency of an LLM to generate
responses that align with a user's stated or implied beliefs at the expense of
truthfulness~\citep{sharma2023understanding}, with \citet{malmqvist2024sycophancy} framing it as
excessive agreement or flattery that threatens reliability and ethical deployment.
\citet{cheng2026elephant} broaden the construct with \emph{social sycophancy}, the excessive
preservation of the user's face: affirmation of choices, judgments, and identity even when clearly
problematic, and avoidance of any response that might offend.

\begin{table}[ht]
\centering
\caption{Primary sycophancy types and definitions.}
\label{tab:taxonomy}
\small
\begin{tabular}{@{}p{1.5cm}p{0.39\linewidth}p{0.29\linewidth}@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{Type} & \textbf{Description} & \textbf{Example} \\
\midrule
Propositional & Affirming user beliefs (even if false) at the expense of accuracy &
  Agreeing that a historical date is correct when it is not \\
Social & Preserving user face through validation, flattery, or avoidance of disagreement &
  Endorsing a user's poor decision to maintain rapport \\
Progressive & Yielding to user pressure when the user happens to be correct &
  Arriving at the right answer only after pushback \\
Regressive & Yielding to user pressure when the user is incorrect &
  Abandoning a correct answer due to user displeasure \\
Subtle / implicit & Selective framing, omission of contrary evidence, or deferential hedging &
  Mentioning only evidence that supports the user's view \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

The most systematic organization to date is the two-axis framework \citet{ye2026taxonomy} derive
from their 70-paper review. Their \emph{referent} axis asks whether the model responds to the
user's expressed positions, verifiable or subjective, or to the user as a person, through traits or
emotions; we call these propositional and social sycophancy and the axis \emph{target}, although
they place part of social sycophancy as \citet{cheng2026elephant} define it under subjective
positions. Their \emph{explicitness} axis, our \emph{directness}, separates overt behavior, such as
outright agreement with a false claim, from implicit behavior through framing, omission, or tone.
The covert half of this axis is only
beginning to be measured, by instruments for implicit sycophancy in mental-health
dialogue~\citep{han2026implicit} and for split beliefs in vision-language
models~\citep{hong2026visual}.

Within propositional sycophancy, outcome matters. \citet{fanous2025syceval} distinguish
\emph{progressive} sycophancy, capitulation that lands on the correct answer, from
\emph{regressive} sycophancy, capitulation that lands on an incorrect one, observing rates of
43.52\% and 14.66\% respectively in their benchmark. Progressive capitulation may be appropriate
updating when the user corrects a genuine model error; regressive capitulation is unconditionally
harmful, and aggregate metrics that merge the two overstate harm in domains where users are often
right. The split presupposes a correctness label, so it exists only for the 26 of 44 dedicated
instruments that have one (Section~\ref{subsec:reftypes}). A terminological caution applies: parts of the literature use progressive for the temporal
pattern of gradual capitulation across turns. Throughout this SoK, including the glossary in
Appendix~\ref{app:glossary}, the pair is reserved strictly for outcome, following
\citet{fanous2025syceval}, and the temporal phenomenon is described as incremental or
accelerating capitulation (Section~\ref{subsec:multiturn}).

The taxonomy is not merely descriptive; its classes are mechanistically distinct.
\citet{vennemeyer2025notone} show through activation analysis across multiple models that
sycophantic agreement and sycophantic praise are encoded along distinct linear directions that can
be amplified or suppressed independently, so an intervention that targets one form may leave
others intact. This single finding constrains every mitigation claim in
Section~\ref{sec:controls}.

Sycophancy is related to, but distinct from, adjacent failure modes.
Hallucination~\citep{ji2023hallucination} is not necessarily aligned with any user belief, whereas
sycophantic content is directionally biased toward the user; the two co-occur when a model
agreeing with a false premise hallucinates supporting detail. \citet{burns2022latent} show that
models often encode the accurate answer internally while producing false output, suggesting
suppression of latent knowledge rather than its absence. Specification
gaming~\citep{amodei2016concrete} and reward hacking~\citep{skalse2022reward} are the umbrella
phenomena: the Proxy Compression Hypothesis of \citet{wang2026pch} unifies sycophancy, verbosity
bias, and hallucinated justification as exploitations of the information lost when human
objectives are compressed into a scalar reward, and \citet{denison2024subterfuge} show the same
gaming can escalate to reward tampering.
